iness  impact of the ml use cases again so you  can make sure that you're justifying  your investment in the ml project after  that you can create your ml roadmap for  development and we'll talk a little bit  more about how to do that later on so as  you're starting to think about ml and  where to begin I want you to consider  where you are on this path to ml and  this path is really the journey that any  process or product might go through as  its maturing so I'm going to walk  through one example related to a contact  center or support team but you can think  about any process or product in the same  way so if you have a new contact center  at first you may receive requests from  customers and you may only have one  person answering the phone I know a lot  of startups begin this way  but over time as you get more and more  requests from customers you'll move out  of that individual contributor phase and  into the next step which is around  delegation you might need a team of  people to respond to those customer  support requests and that is phase two  of delegation during this phase there'll  be a lot of standardization that happens  of your business processes so that  anyone can actually perform that role  after that we often see customers move  into this digitization phase so this  will be where you'll maybe set up a  ticketing system to automate and help  digitize those support requests the  routing the solution and this is an  important step because it really  liberate and starts to collect a lot of  the data that in the past you maybe  weren't capturing in any sort of  meaningful way and over time as you  acquire more and more data you move into  this big data and analytics base and  sometimes you might stay in this phase  and that's okay but sometimes you may  want to do something more sophisticated  again especially when you're making  repeated decisions so you might want to  move into this machine learning phase so  with this contact center example you may